#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0393 expect=violation domain=TS
#note "THE SCOPE-WIDENING PIN (Fix #301 / M3-D23(ii)). TS is a TRIAL DESIGN dataset whose columns are declared in a deliberately wrong order (TSVAL before TSPARMCD) against the sidecar's model order. Before M3-D23 the rule carried `Scope.Classes.Include: [FINDINGS, INTERVENTIONS, EVENTS]` and this dataset was SKIPPED on the class axis. Sheet rows 1906-1907 read Class='ALL', Domain='ALL', Variable='ALL', and four same-shaped cross-family relatives -- CDISC-CG0330, CDISC-CG0664, FDA-SD1079, PMDA-SD1079 -- all carry Scope.Domains.Include [ALL]; the narrowing had no basis. With the Classes block replaced by Domains.Include [ALL] the rule reaches TS and reports the disorder. ESCALATE if this reports SKIPPED: the scope replacement is not in effect."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
#library model-column-order TS STUDYID DOMAIN TSSEQ TSPARMCD TSPARM TSVAL
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset TS class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col TSSEQ    type=Num
col TSVAL    type=Char
col TSPARMCD type=Char
---
S1 | TS | 1 | A Study | TITLE
---
